<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15526" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ēlongo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a. and n.
		e-longe. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to remove</i>, <i>keep aloof</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auxilium tuum a me,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Psa. 21, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">judicium a nobis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Isa. 59, 9 al.</span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>To prolong</i>, <i>protract</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">diem ejus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Isa. 14, 1</span></i>
			; cf. elongo, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μακρύνω,
			ἀφίστημι</span>, Gloss. Philox.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to withdraw</i>, <i>depart</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ecce elongavi fugiens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Psa. 54, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Sir. 35, 22</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Jer. 2,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Luc. 3, §
			32</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
